## 📖 Detailed File Extraction Procedures

### 1. Generating Specifications (`specifications.md`)
1. Open your target dashboard in Google Sheets Canvas.
2. Open `sandbox/dashboards/<dashboard-name>/reverse-prompt-<feature-name>.md` and copy its full content.
3. Paste the prompt into Gemini Canvas (or your LLM analyzer) pointing to the dashboard sheet.
4. Copy the complete 7-module Markdown response and save it to:
   `sandbox/dashboards/<dashboard-name>/specifications.md` (replacing `specifications.md.wait`).

### 2. Exporting Dataset (`<dashboard-name>-data.csv`)
1. In Google Sheets, navigate to the active sheet containing your raw/consolidated dashboard data.
2. Select **File > Download > Comma-separated values (.csv)**.
3. Move/rename the downloaded file to:
   `sandbox/dashboards/<dashboard-name>/<dashboard-name>-data.csv` (replacing `<dashboard-name>-data.csv.wait`).

### 3. Exporting HTML DOM Layout (`iframe-html/<dashboard-name>.html`)
1. Open Google Sheets in Google Chrome and press `F12` (or Right Click > Inspect) to open **Chrome Developer Tools**.
2. In the Elements panel, locate the root `<iframe>` element containing the canvas or select its inner `<html>` element.
3. Right-click the element and select **Edit as HTML** (or **Copy > Copy element**).
4. Copy the full HTML payload and save it to:
   `sandbox/dashboards/<dashboard-name>/iframe-html/<dashboard-name>.html` (replacing `<dashboard-name>.html.wait`).

---

## 📁 Canonical React Feature Target Directory Layout

The generated React clone strictly follows the canonical feature pattern defined in `reverse-prompt-<feature-name>.template.md`:

```text
src/
├── components/
│   └── ui/                               # Primitive UI (Shadcn Base UI: Button, Modal, Checkbox, Tooltip, Badge, Input)
├── features/
│   ├── `<feature-name/>`/                # Main feature component folder
│   │   ├── `<FeatureName/>Feature.tsx`   # Main feature entry point, organize Global layout. import `<FeatureName/>Panel`
│   │   ├── `<FeatureName/>Panel.tsx`     # Panel layout, import `<FeatureName/>`Header, `<FeatureName/>`Grid, `<FeatureName/>`Footer, ...
│   │   ├── components/                   # `<FeatureName/>`Header, `<FeatureName/>`Grid, VirtualTable, KPI, Cards
│   │   │   └── tabs/                     # `TabName01`Tab, `TabName02`Tab, ...
│   │   ├── hooks/                        # use`<FeatureName/>`Handlers.ts, use`<FeatureName/>`State.ts, ...
│   │   ├── store/                        # use`<FeatureName/>`Store.ts (Pure In-Memory Zustand Store)
│   │   ├── model/                        # `<FeatureName/>` UI interfaces models
│   │   ├── types/                        # types.ts (enums and types definitions)
│   │   └── utils/                        # utility functions (Converters, Data Pipelines, Coordinate Parsers, FormulaDAG, SecuritySanitizer, etc.)
├── styles/                               # Global styles, TailwindCSS v4 config, and design tokens
├── services/                             # API services, data ingestion, and validation pipelines
└── utils/                                # transformers, sanitizers, and shared utility functions
```

---

## 🚀 How to Start Using This Orchestrator

1. In VS Code, open a new Copilot AI chat session.
2. Select the `@gsheet-to-react-orchestrator` agent.
3. Enter: `@gsheet-to-react-orchestrator Start cloning my dashboard "<GSHEET_DASHBOARD_CANVAS_NAME>"` to start the migration process.

The orchestrator will automatically configure target folders with `.wait` placeholders, generate the reverse engineering prompt, and guide you turn-by-turn.

---

# 😎 User-Guide

### 🎭 End-to-End Workflow Simulation

Below is the step-by-step simulation of how a developer interacts with the Orchestrator Agent.

---

#### 🎬 TURN 1 — Initial Request (User Input)

**User Input:**

> `@gsheet-to-react-orchestrator Start cloning my dashboard "sales-kpi-dashboard" using localStorage persistence`

**Agent Execution (Automated Steps 1, 2 & 3):**

1. **Step 1 (Smart Config Setup):**
   * Extracts `<dashboard-name>` = `sales-kpi-dashboard`.
   * Registers `STORE_DESTINATION_TARGET` = `localStorage`.
   * Creates workspace directory structure and `.wait` placeholder files:
     ```bash
     mkdir -p sandbox/dashboards/sales-kpi-dashboard/agent/
     mkdir -p sandbox/dashboards/sales-kpi-dashboard/iframe-html/
     touch sandbox/dashboards/sales-kpi-dashboard/specifications.md.wait
     touch sandbox/dashboards/sales-kpi-dashboard/sales-kpi-dashboard-data.csv.wait
     touch sandbox/dashboards/sales-kpi-dashboard/iframe-html/sales-kpi-dashboard.html.wait
     ```
   * Initializes `sandbox/dashboards/sales-kpi-dashboard/agent/plan-follower.md`.

2. **Step 2 (Reverse Engineering Prompt Generation):**
   * Calls skill `gsheet-react-dashboard-reverse`.
   * Writes the full reverse prompt to `sandbox/dashboards/sales-kpi-dashboard/reverse-prompt-sales-kpi-dashboard.md`.

3. **Step 3 (Batch Artifact Collection Gate):**
   * Displays target paths with `.wait` placeholders and stops output to await user confirmation.

**Agent Response Output:**

> ### 📋 Plan Initialized: `sales-kpi-dashboard`
>
> Target Store Model: `localStorage`
>
> Reverse prompt generated at: `sandbox/dashboards/sales-kpi-dashboard/reverse-prompt-sales-kpi-dashboard.md`
>
> ---
>
> ### 📥 Batch Asset Collection Gate
>
> Placeholder files (`.wait`) have been created in `sandbox/dashboards/sales-kpi-dashboard/`. Please save or replace the 3 authoritative source artifacts at these paths:
>
> 1. **Specifications Markdown:** Save to `sandbox/dashboards/sales-kpi-dashboard/specifications.md`
> 2. **CSV Data:** Save to `sandbox/dashboards/sales-kpi-dashboard/sales-kpi-dashboard-data.csv`
> 3. **HTML DOM Export:** Save to `sandbox/dashboards/sales-kpi-dashboard/iframe-html/sales-kpi-dashboard.html`
>
> 👉 **Action Required:** Once all 3 files are saved, reply in chat with **`Confirm Artifacts Saved`**!

---

#### 🎬 TURN 2 — Artifact Drop & Blueprint Generation (User Input)

**User Action:**

* User drops the 3 requested files into the `sandbox/dashboards/sales-kpi-dashboard/` folder.
* User replies in chat: **`Confirm Artifacts Saved`**

**Agent Execution (Automated Steps 4 & 5a):**

1. **Step 4 (Auto HTML Split & Co-location):**
   * Executes `html-split/run-split.sh` to extract `styles.css`, `script.js`, and cleaned HTML.

2. **Step 5a (Cloner Stage 1 Blueprint):**
   * Invokes `gsheet-react-dashboard-cloner` with `STORE_DESTINATION_TARGET = localStorage`.
   * Produces Stage 1 Evidence Audit, Conflict Reconciliation, Abstract Model IR, and Zustand Store Blueprints.
   * Updates `plan-follower.md`.

**Agent Response Output:**

> ### 🎨 Asset Extraction Complete
> HTML/CSS split executed successfully. Design tokens and scripts co-located in `sandbox/dashboards/sales-kpi-dashboard/iframe-html/`.
>
> ### 🏗️ Stage 1 Architecture Blueprint
> [Displays Evidence Audit Matrix, Conflict Log, and Zustand Store Blueprint]
>
> 👉 **Action Required:** Reply in chat with **`GENERATE CODEBASE`** to compile the React application!

---

#### 🎬 TURN 3 — Full Codebase Compilation & Verification (User Input)

**User Action:**

* User replies in chat: **`GENERATE CODEBASE`**

**Agent Execution (Automated Steps 5b & 6):**

1. **Step 5b (Codebase Compilation):**
   * Emits complete, fully typed multi-file React feature strictly matching the canonical directory structure into `sandbox/dashboards/sales-kpi-dashboard/react-clone/`.

2. **Step 6 (Build Verification & Final Handoff):**
   * Runs `npm run build` inside `sandbox/dashboards/sales-kpi-dashboard/react-clone/`.
   * Updates `plan-follower.md` to `COMPLETED` for all 6 steps.

**Agent Response Output:**

> ### ✅ React Codebase Successfully Generated & Verified
> All components have been compiled into `sandbox/dashboards/sales-kpi-dashboard/react-clone/` matching the canonical modular React feature structure.
>
> #### 📁 Component File Hierarchy
> * 🚀 Main Entry Point: `sandbox/dashboards/sales-kpi-dashboard/react-clone/src/features/sales-kpi-dashboard/SalesKpiDashboardFeature.tsx`
> * 🏪 State Store: `sandbox/dashboards/sales-kpi-dashboard/react-clone/src/features/sales-kpi-dashboard/store/useSalesKpiDashboardStore.ts`
> * 🎨 Scoped CSS: `sandbox/dashboards/sales-kpi-dashboard/react-clone/src/styles/index.css`
